{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BdADAXjukTT9T89E7ntkBK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"mck1117 atlas ECU brain module github CAN termination\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"can terminator pack\",\"url\":\"https://docs.revrobotics.com/ion-control/accessories/can-terminator-pack\"},{\"title\":\"MCU1 LED Control ECU (Arduino Uno + MCP2515)\",\"url\":\"https://sdv-blueprints.eclipse.dev/docs/e2e-demo-blueprint/device-led-ecu\"},{\"title\":\"canbed arduino compatible can bus development kit online\",\"url\":\"https://thinkrobotics.com/es/products/canbed-arduino-compatible-can-bus-development-kit-online\"},{\"title\":\"CAN module - SN65HVD230\",\"url\":\"https://www.rusefi.com/forum/viewtopic.php?p=4907\"},{\"title\":\"CAN module - SN65HVD230\",\"url\":\"https://rusefi.com/forum/viewtopic.php?p=5831\"},{\"title\":\"# Arduino MKR CAN Shield\",\"url\":\"https://core-electronics.com.au/arduino-mkr-can-shield-44918.html.plain.md\"},{\"title\":\"can controller\",\"url\":\"https://gbmc.googlesource.com/linux/+/7b2e57c26d45d55aa00d9f2904db12633596ffdb/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/can/can-controller.yaml\"},{\"title\":\"CAN termination resistor\",\"url\":\"https://forum.opencyphal.org/t/can-termination-resistor/289\"},{\"title\":\"Smart controller area network termination\",\"url\":\"https://patents.justia.com/patent/11394579\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up the mck1117 Atlas ECU repository or any of its documentation about CAN termination. None of the results mention Atlas or mck1117, so I couldn't confirm how that project handles termination.\n\nThe results do cover general CAN termination practice:\n\n- **Standard value:** One result states that both physical endpoints of the CAN bus must be capped with terminating resistances, and that these are usually placed on the first and last nodes of the bus (index 9-8).\n- **Resistor value:** A forum post notes that 120 ohm termination is expected at the end of CAN bus nodes, and a hardware guide recommends twisted-pair wiring with 120 Ω resistors at each end of the bus.\n- **Switchable options:** Some boards include an onboard resistor that can be switched in or out, and one rusEFI forum thread discusses adding a termination jumper (index 4-8).\n\nFor the Atlas-specific details, check the project's GitHub README, wiring diagrams, or issue tracker directly, or run a narrower search for the repository name.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a5d128e-ff0a-47b7-9b33-ea39fb44a264","uuid":"35d8afaa-df52-4d17-9c21-68ae115a00d0","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:32:25.501Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"mck1117 atlas ECU brain module github CAN termination","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01TvPk7wERwdMRaxpnE2Ucff","content":[{"title":"can terminator pack","url":"https://docs.revrobotics.com/ion-control/accessories/can-terminator-pack"},{"title":"MCU1 LED Control ECU (Arduino Uno + MCP2515)","url":"https://sdv-blueprints.eclipse.dev/docs/e2e-demo-blueprint/device-led-ecu"},{"title":"canbed arduino compatible can bus development kit online","url":"https://thinkrobotics.com/es/products/canbed-arduino-compatible-can-bus-development-kit-online"},{"title":"CAN module - SN65HVD230","url":"https://www.rusefi.com/forum/viewtopic.php?p=4907"},{"title":"CAN module - SN65HVD230","url":"https://rusefi.com/forum/viewtopic.php?p=5831"},{"title":"# Arduino MKR CAN Shield","url":"https://core-electronics.com.au/arduino-mkr-can-shield-44918.html.plain.md"},{"title":"can controller","url":"https://gbmc.googlesource.com/linux/+/7b2e57c26d45d55aa00d9f2904db12633596ffdb/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/can/can-controller.yaml"},{"title":"CAN termination resistor","url":"https://forum.opencyphal.org/t/can-termination-resistor/289"},{"title":"Smart controller area network termination","url":"https://patents.justia.com/patent/11394579"}]},"The search didn't turn up the mck1117 Atlas ECU repository or any of its documentation about CAN termination. None of the results mention Atlas or mck1117, so I couldn't confirm how that project handles termination.\n\nThe results do cover general CAN termination practice:\n\n- **Standard value:** One result states that both physical endpoints of the CAN bus must be capped with terminating resistances, and that these are usually placed on the first and last nodes of the bus (index 9-8).\n- **Resistor value:** A forum post notes that 120 ohm termination is expected at the end of CAN bus nodes, and a hardware guide recommends twisted-pair wiring with 120 Ω resistors at each end of the bus.\n- **Switchable options:** Some boards include an onboard resistor that can be switched in or out, and one rusEFI forum thread discusses adding a termination jumper (index 4-8).\n\nFor the Atlas-specific details, check the project's GitHub README, wiring diagrams, or issue tracker directly, or run a narrower search for the repository name."],"durationSeconds":5.401491299999995,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BdADAXjukTT9T89E7ntkBK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
