{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cg6sp2RKh9pPoMoQ7xuzk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0146TzgdHaoyDBCHu5YPVrt1","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidate_id":"46e5a5c34e7b9715155c9e90277cd3639b3a19ebb9590053a081bbb6436ba860","run_id":"8534a2a6-e237-4d1c-a002-90ce37ec09e4","packet_sha256":"98d9c1b6fab29738035a23626c8f92708bf9cb153628d6077ab0ca2e6b9f0340","role":"circuit","schema":"agent-ee.review/1","coverage":["Reproduced native ERC and DRC with kicad-cli 10.0.7 against the read-only candidate; all 5 ERC errors, all 13 DRC errors, 0 unconnected items and 114 parity issues match the packet (library-availability warning counts differ only with environment).","Triaged every error-severity ERC violation (3x power_pin_not_driven, pin_not_connected on A1 ~FLT, pin_to_pin on J2 pins 40/41) against the netlist and harness power entry paths.","Triaged every error-severity DRC violation (5x padstack + 5x annular_width on J1 mechanical peg holes, 3x starved_thermal on GND pads C14/C15/U7).","Scoped CAN2 termination review: confirmed R36/R37 (120R) both DNP in schematic and saved board with 'n.p.' annotation; enumerated all CAN2 bus members; fetched FOME-Tech/Polygonus sources and wire-traced the module's populated 120R (R10) across CANH2/CANL2; computed recessive-settling RC for terminated (~10 ns) and hypothetical unterminated (~0.7-1.6 us vs 2 us bit) cases.","Verified TJA1051T/3 pin identity (TXD/GND/VCC/RXD/VIO/CANL/CANH/S), S=GND normal mode, VCC=5V, VIO=3.3V matching the 3.3V-logic f042 wideband modules, and correct CAN_RX/CAN_TX pairing to both wideband modules; verified distinct SEL ID straps on U1 vs U2.","Verified TLE9201SG pin 2 = VSO tied to +3.3V against the Infineon datasheet; DIS default-disable pull-ups; VS/outputs wiring.","Verified DRV8825 carrier strapping (nRESET/nSLEEP high, mode/nENABLE low, VMOT bulk cap) and confirmed from Polygonus mcu.kicad_sch that LS9-12 are 3.3V push-pull MCU outputs, so STEP/DIR and VNL5090 adder drive levels exceed input thresholds (no 2.5V divider marginality).","Verified VR module 74HC02 cross-coupled NOR latch topology, grounded unused gates, and MAX9924 VR-conditioner bias/output network; checked local '+5V' label merge into the single global +5V net in connectivity.json.","Verified the disposable sheet alias: 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' is byte-identical (sha256 377a2691...) to 'VR conditioner.kicad_sch', root references the alias, and the netlist resolves the full 10-sheet hierarchy including all VR Conditioner components."],"limitations":["Atlas brain-module compatibility (claimed in inputs/project/README.md) could not be assessed: github.com/mck1117/atlas returns 404, so CAN2 termination with an Atlas module installed is unverified.","Polygonus module evidence is upstream master-branch source, not necessarily the exact revision matching this donor.","No SPICE simulation was run (no vendor models for TJA1051/MAX9924/TLE9201 at hand); CAN timing is an analytic RC estimate recorded in review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md.","Power budget (fuse F1 sizing, wideband heater and ETB currents through J1 pins and F1), connector pin current ratings, ignition energy, EMC, thermal and automotive transient behavior were not evaluated (also outside packet scope).","Zone fill evaluated as saved; the read-only candidate forbids a refill pass.","MAX9924 CRANK+/CRANK- polarity swap relative to the typical application circuit was observed but not adjudicated: no stated requirement fixes the intended edge polarity, and firmware edge selection can absorb it."],"findings":[{"id":"circ-01-can2-termination-dnp","title":"Internal wideband CAN2 bus has no termination populated on the base board; function depends entirely on the plug-in brain module","location":"project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch (R36/R37, 'n.p.' text at 113.03,76.2); board R36 at (175.01,140.67), R37 at (81.62,140.55)","condition":"Both 120R terminators R36 and R37 are DNP ((dnp yes), in_bom no) in both instances of the WBO-CAN-TRANS sheet, and no other termination exists anywhere on the base board's /CAN2+ //CAN2- nets, which carry three transceiver nodes (U20, U21, brain-module CAN2 via J2.73/74), ~94 pF per line of filter capacitance (duplicated 47 pF C29/C33 and C30/C34), ESD clamps D10/D11, and harness pins J1.15/J1.11.","mechanism":"A CAN bus with zero resistive termination relies on transceiver input bias (TJA1051 R_i(cm) 15-37 kOhm/pin; ~10-25 kOhm differential for three nodes) to return to recessive; with ~80 pF effective differential capacitance the settling constant is ~0.7-1.6 us against a 2 us bit at 500 kbit/s, so dominant-to-recessive edges do not settle and the advertised internal dual-wideband link fails or is marginal. I verified the primary configuration is saved from this: the Polygonus brain module itself carries one populated 120R (R10 wired across CANH2/CANL2 next to MCP2551 U5 in Polygonus psu.kicad_sch), giving a single-terminated short bus (tau ~10 ns, functional). However the README also claims Atlas module compatibility, and the Atlas design is unreachable (404), so an installed module without on-module termination would leave the internal bus completely unterminated with no base-board default protecting against it.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol R36 (dnp yes)/(in_bom no), value 120, pins on CAN2+/CAN2- wires at y=83.82/88.9; text \"n.p.\" at (113.03,76.2)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2- listing U20.7/6, U21.7/6, J2.73/74, J1.15/11, D10/D11, C29/C30/C33/C34, R36/R37; dnp_refs include R36,R37"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 4: Polygonus R10 120R wire trace in psu.kicad_sch and RC settling calculations"},{"path":"inputs/project/README.md","locator":"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... connected internally to CAN bus #2'; compatibility claim for Polygonus and Atlas"}],"reasoning":"The scoped question resolves as: termination exists but only on the removable brain module, verified by independent retrieval and wire-tracing of the Polygonus source, not on the reviewed board. Single 120R termination on a short internal bus is electrically adequate (calculation in experiments), so this is not a defect of the saved design in its documented primary configuration; it is a configuration-dependence concern because the base board as built provides zero termination and the second claimed-compatible module family could not be verified."},{"id":"circ-02-erc-errors","title":"Schematic fails native ERC with 5 errors (power modeling and unused pins); no electrical malfunction identified","location":"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch root sheet (A1, J2, #PWR01)","condition":"ERC reports: Input Power pin not driven for #PWR01 GND, A1 pin 8 VMOT (/12V_MR_FUSE), and J2 pin 90 12V_IGN (/12V_KEY); pin_not_connected for A1 pin 2 ~FLT; pin_to_pin error for J2 pins 40/41 (two 'Power output' pins tied together). Reproduced exactly in an independent ERC run.","mechanism":"The supply nets are fed only through passive connector pins (J1.105/106 through fuse F1; J1.45) with no PWR_FLAG, so KiCad cannot prove the power-input pins are driven; A1's open-drain fault output is deliberately unused; J2 pins 40/41 are paralleled outputs of the same module regulator modeled as two power-output pins. None of these indicates a wiring fault - battery and key power genuinely arrive via the harness - but the design does not pass its own native ruleset as saved, and standing errors can mask future real regressions.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"error entries: power_pin_not_driven at (36.83,78.74), (48.26,219.71), (293.37,173.99); pin_not_connected at (38.1,224.79); pin_to_pin at (262.89,128.27/130.81)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"/12V_MR_FUSE containing F1.2, J1.73/74, A1.8; /12V_KEY = J1.45, J2.90; /5V_SENSOR_1 = J1.16/19/20, J2.40, J2.41"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"sections 1-2: ERC reproduction (identical 5 errors) and triage"}],"reasoning":"A native violation is a reportable defect even when benign; I verified each error's electrical context from the netlist and found power sourcing and intentional no-connects rather than faults, hence minor severity rather than functional."},{"id":"circ-03-j1-mechanical-pth-padstack","title":"J1 connector mounting peg holes modeled as plated pads with zero annular ring (5 padstack + 5 annular-width DRC errors)","location":"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, footprint Simon:Molex_112_643330100 (J1 at 133.2,43.34)","condition":"Five unnumbered thru-hole pads in the J1 footprint have pad size equal to drill (4.0/4.0 mm and 2.2/2.2 mm, e.g. at (71.95,35.49), (120.0,28.49), (203.25,35.49)), producing DRC errors 'PTH pad hole leaves no copper' and 'annular width 0.0000 mm' against the 0.1 mm board constraint.","mechanism":"Connector alignment/retention pegs defined as PTH with no copper ring should be NPTH; as saved they request plated holes with no annulus, which fabricators commonly flag or silently convert, and plating slivers in a ringless hole can flake. No net is attached, so there is no connectivity or electrical impact.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"error-severity 'padstack' and 'annular_width' entries, items 'PTH pad [<no net>] of J1' at the five listed coordinates"},{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"(not applicable to this finding; see board file)"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 3: extraction of the five unnumbered pads with size==drill from the saved board file"}],"reasoning":"Verified directly in the saved board that pad diameter equals drill on unconnected mechanical holes; this is a footprint-modeling/fabrication-interface defect, not an electrical one, hence minor."},{"id":"circ-04-starved-thermals","title":"Three GND pads receive only one of two required thermal spokes from the GND zone","location":"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, F.Cu GND zone; pads C15.2 (107.85,98.76), U7.4 (101.01,102.68), C14.2 (101.59,104.29)","condition":"DRC error 'Thermal relief connection to zone incomplete (zone min spoke count 2; actual 1)' on the GND pads of decoupling caps C15/C14 and comparator U7 in the VR-module area, in the saved (unrefilled) zone fill.","mechanism":"A single-spoke thermal connection remains electrically connected (0 unconnected items) but halves the pad's copper connection, raising connection impedance for a comparator ground/decoupling path and reducing solder-joint and rework robustness; a refill or local keepout fix would be needed, which the read-only review cannot apply.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"three error-severity 'starved_thermal' entries listing Zone [GND] on F.Cu/B.Cu/In2.Gnd.Cu and pads C15.2, U7.4, C14.2"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"sections 1,3: independent DRC reproduction (same 3 starved_thermal errors) and triage"}],"reasoning":"Reproduced independently; connectivity is intact so impact is manufacturing robustness and marginally higher ground-connection impedance on small-signal parts, consistent with minor severity."},{"id":"circ-05-sheet-alias-duplicate","title":"Hierarchy resolved via byte-identical case-variant duplicate sheet file; divergence and case-collision hazard remains","location":"project/VR Conditioner.kicad_sch vs project/VR conditioner.kicad_sch; root reference at Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch line 21553","condition":"The candidate contains two sheet files whose names differ only by case, verified byte-identical (sha256 377a2691ec878301977100851c40e302b2b7864d88cc27c6c305c03bbf14e15b for both); the root schematic references 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' and the netlist resolves all VR-conditioner components through it.","mechanism":"The alias makes the 10-sheet hierarchy complete for this review (confirmed: U10/JP1/C23-C25/R25-R34 present in the netlist), but future edits through KiCad update only the referenced file, letting the lowercase copy silently go stale, and checkouts on case-insensitive filesystems (Windows/macOS defaults) will collide the two names. The packet itself declares this is a disposable alias and the original discrepancy remains open.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 6: matching sha256 of both files and root Sheetfile reference at line 21553"},{"path":"work/netlist/design.xml","locator":"sheet number 4 '/VR Conditioner/' with source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"components C23-C25, R25-R34, U10, JP1 with sheet '/VR Conditioner/'"}],"reasoning":"Verified the alias is a faithful byte copy and that connectivity is currently correct, so no electrical defect; recorded as info-level configuration-management concern consistent with the packet's declared limitation."},{"id":"circ-06-max9924-input-polarity","title":"VR1 (MAX9924) differential inputs wired with CRANK+ to IN- and CRANK- to IN+ (inverted vs. typical application)","location":"project/VR Conditioner.kicad_sch (U10 MAX9924, R25/R27 and R26/R28 input chains)","condition":"Netlist shows /CRANK + (J1.59) -> R25 4.7k -> R27 4.7k -> U10.2 (IN-) and /CRANK - (J1.55) -> R26 4.7k -> R28 4.7k -> U10.1 (IN+), the opposite of the MAX9924 typical application polarity.","mechanism":"Swapped differential polarity inverts the comparator output edge relative to the VR sensor's true tooth-edge zero crossing. ECU firmware edge selection can absorb a static inversion, and adaptive-threshold zero-cross detection is symmetric, so this does not necessarily impair function; but if firmware assumes the conventional polarity, trigger edges land on the wrong tooth flank, degrading timing accuracy on asymmetric VR waveforms.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets '/CRANK +': [J1.59, R25.2]; 'Net-(R25-Pad1)': [R25.1, R27.2]; 'Net-(U10-IN-)': [C23.1, R27.1, R29.2, U10.2]; '/CRANK -': [J1.55, R26.2]; 'Net-(U10-IN+)': [C23.2, R28.1, R29.1, U10.1]"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 5: MAX9924 wiring observation and rationale"}],"reasoning":"The cross-wiring is evidenced directly in the exported netlist, but no stated requirement fixes the intended polarity and the donor is an established design whose firmware pairing is out of scope, so this is recorded as an info-level concern for human confirmation rather than a defect."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6347,"cache_read_input_tokens":337641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6347},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a5d128e-ff0a-47b7-9b33-ea39fb44a264","uuid":"9bcfb6b7-549f-454e-a6a1-6d510f322363","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:40:36.802Z","request_id":"req_011Cg6sp29hoLcdXSCuRnHzA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0146TzgdHaoyDBCHu5YPVrt1":{"candidate_id":"46e5a5c34e7b9715155c9e90277cd3639b3a19ebb9590053a081bbb6436ba860","run_id":"8534a2a6-e237-4d1c-a002-90ce37ec09e4","packet_sha256":"98d9c1b6fab29738035a23626c8f92708bf9cb153628d6077ab0ca2e6b9f0340","role":"circuit","schema":"agent-ee.review/1","coverage":["Reproduced native ERC and DRC with kicad-cli 10.0.7 against the read-only candidate; all 5 ERC errors, all 13 DRC errors, 0 unconnected items and 114 parity issues match the packet (library-availability warning counts differ only with environment).","Triaged every error-severity ERC violation (3x power_pin_not_driven, pin_not_connected on A1 ~FLT, pin_to_pin on J2 pins 40/41) against the netlist and harness power entry paths.","Triaged every error-severity DRC violation (5x padstack + 5x annular_width on J1 mechanical peg holes, 3x starved_thermal on GND pads C14/C15/U7).","Scoped CAN2 termination review: confirmed R36/R37 (120R) both DNP in schematic and saved board with 'n.p.' annotation; enumerated all CAN2 bus members; fetched FOME-Tech/Polygonus sources and wire-traced the module's populated 120R (R10) across CANH2/CANL2; computed recessive-settling RC for terminated (~10 ns) and hypothetical unterminated (~0.7-1.6 us vs 2 us bit) cases.","Verified TJA1051T/3 pin identity (TXD/GND/VCC/RXD/VIO/CANL/CANH/S), S=GND normal mode, VCC=5V, VIO=3.3V matching the 3.3V-logic f042 wideband modules, and correct CAN_RX/CAN_TX pairing to both wideband modules; verified distinct SEL ID straps on U1 vs U2.","Verified TLE9201SG pin 2 = VSO tied to +3.3V against the Infineon datasheet; DIS default-disable pull-ups; VS/outputs wiring.","Verified DRV8825 carrier strapping (nRESET/nSLEEP high, mode/nENABLE low, VMOT bulk cap) and confirmed from Polygonus mcu.kicad_sch that LS9-12 are 3.3V push-pull MCU outputs, so STEP/DIR and VNL5090 adder drive levels exceed input thresholds (no 2.5V divider marginality).","Verified VR module 74HC02 cross-coupled NOR latch topology, grounded unused gates, and MAX9924 VR-conditioner bias/output network; checked local '+5V' label merge into the single global +5V net in connectivity.json.","Verified the disposable sheet alias: 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' is byte-identical (sha256 377a2691...) to 'VR conditioner.kicad_sch', root references the alias, and the netlist resolves the full 10-sheet hierarchy including all VR Conditioner components."],"limitations":["Atlas brain-module compatibility (claimed in inputs/project/README.md) could not be assessed: github.com/mck1117/atlas returns 404, so CAN2 termination with an Atlas module installed is unverified.","Polygonus module evidence is upstream master-branch source, not necessarily the exact revision matching this donor.","No SPICE simulation was run (no vendor models for TJA1051/MAX9924/TLE9201 at hand); CAN timing is an analytic RC estimate recorded in review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md.","Power budget (fuse F1 sizing, wideband heater and ETB currents through J1 pins and F1), connector pin current ratings, ignition energy, EMC, thermal and automotive transient behavior were not evaluated (also outside packet scope).","Zone fill evaluated as saved; the read-only candidate forbids a refill pass.","MAX9924 CRANK+/CRANK- polarity swap relative to the typical application circuit was observed but not adjudicated: no stated requirement fixes the intended edge polarity, and firmware edge selection can absorb it."],"findings":[{"id":"circ-01-can2-termination-dnp","title":"Internal wideband CAN2 bus has no termination populated on the base board; function depends entirely on the plug-in brain module","location":"project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch (R36/R37, 'n.p.' text at 113.03,76.2); board R36 at (175.01,140.67), R37 at (81.62,140.55)","condition":"Both 120R terminators R36 and R37 are DNP ((dnp yes), in_bom no) in both instances of the WBO-CAN-TRANS sheet, and no other termination exists anywhere on the base board's /CAN2+ //CAN2- nets, which carry three transceiver nodes (U20, U21, brain-module CAN2 via J2.73/74), ~94 pF per line of filter capacitance (duplicated 47 pF C29/C33 and C30/C34), ESD clamps D10/D11, and harness pins J1.15/J1.11.","mechanism":"A CAN bus with zero resistive termination relies on transceiver input bias (TJA1051 R_i(cm) 15-37 kOhm/pin; ~10-25 kOhm differential for three nodes) to return to recessive; with ~80 pF effective differential capacitance the settling constant is ~0.7-1.6 us against a 2 us bit at 500 kbit/s, so dominant-to-recessive edges do not settle and the advertised internal dual-wideband link fails or is marginal. I verified the primary configuration is saved from this: the Polygonus brain module itself carries one populated 120R (R10 wired across CANH2/CANL2 next to MCP2551 U5 in Polygonus psu.kicad_sch), giving a single-terminated short bus (tau ~10 ns, functional). However the README also claims Atlas module compatibility, and the Atlas design is unreachable (404), so an installed module without on-module termination would leave the internal bus completely unterminated with no base-board default protecting against it.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol R36 (dnp yes)/(in_bom no), value 120, pins on CAN2+/CAN2- wires at y=83.82/88.9; text \"n.p.\" at (113.03,76.2)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2- listing U20.7/6, U21.7/6, J2.73/74, J1.15/11, D10/D11, C29/C30/C33/C34, R36/R37; dnp_refs include R36,R37"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 4: Polygonus R10 120R wire trace in psu.kicad_sch and RC settling calculations"},{"path":"inputs/project/README.md","locator":"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... connected internally to CAN bus #2'; compatibility claim for Polygonus and Atlas"}],"reasoning":"The scoped question resolves as: termination exists but only on the removable brain module, verified by independent retrieval and wire-tracing of the Polygonus source, not on the reviewed board. Single 120R termination on a short internal bus is electrically adequate (calculation in experiments), so this is not a defect of the saved design in its documented primary configuration; it is a configuration-dependence concern because the base board as built provides zero termination and the second claimed-compatible module family could not be verified."},{"id":"circ-02-erc-errors","title":"Schematic fails native ERC with 5 errors (power modeling and unused pins); no electrical malfunction identified","location":"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch root sheet (A1, J2, #PWR01)","condition":"ERC reports: Input Power pin not driven for #PWR01 GND, A1 pin 8 VMOT (/12V_MR_FUSE), and J2 pin 90 12V_IGN (/12V_KEY); pin_not_connected for A1 pin 2 ~FLT; pin_to_pin error for J2 pins 40/41 (two 'Power output' pins tied together). Reproduced exactly in an independent ERC run.","mechanism":"The supply nets are fed only through passive connector pins (J1.105/106 through fuse F1; J1.45) with no PWR_FLAG, so KiCad cannot prove the power-input pins are driven; A1's open-drain fault output is deliberately unused; J2 pins 40/41 are paralleled outputs of the same module regulator modeled as two power-output pins. None of these indicates a wiring fault - battery and key power genuinely arrive via the harness - but the design does not pass its own native ruleset as saved, and standing errors can mask future real regressions.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"error entries: power_pin_not_driven at (36.83,78.74), (48.26,219.71), (293.37,173.99); pin_not_connected at (38.1,224.79); pin_to_pin at (262.89,128.27/130.81)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"/12V_MR_FUSE containing F1.2, J1.73/74, A1.8; /12V_KEY = J1.45, J2.90; /5V_SENSOR_1 = J1.16/19/20, J2.40, J2.41"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"sections 1-2: ERC reproduction (identical 5 errors) and triage"}],"reasoning":"A native violation is a reportable defect even when benign; I verified each error's electrical context from the netlist and found power sourcing and intentional no-connects rather than faults, hence minor severity rather than functional."},{"id":"circ-03-j1-mechanical-pth-padstack","title":"J1 connector mounting peg holes modeled as plated pads with zero annular ring (5 padstack + 5 annular-width DRC errors)","location":"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, footprint Simon:Molex_112_643330100 (J1 at 133.2,43.34)","condition":"Five unnumbered thru-hole pads in the J1 footprint have pad size equal to drill (4.0/4.0 mm and 2.2/2.2 mm, e.g. at (71.95,35.49), (120.0,28.49), (203.25,35.49)), producing DRC errors 'PTH pad hole leaves no copper' and 'annular width 0.0000 mm' against the 0.1 mm board constraint.","mechanism":"Connector alignment/retention pegs defined as PTH with no copper ring should be NPTH; as saved they request plated holes with no annulus, which fabricators commonly flag or silently convert, and plating slivers in a ringless hole can flake. No net is attached, so there is no connectivity or electrical impact.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"error-severity 'padstack' and 'annular_width' entries, items 'PTH pad [<no net>] of J1' at the five listed coordinates"},{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"(not applicable to this finding; see board file)"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 3: extraction of the five unnumbered pads with size==drill from the saved board file"}],"reasoning":"Verified directly in the saved board that pad diameter equals drill on unconnected mechanical holes; this is a footprint-modeling/fabrication-interface defect, not an electrical one, hence minor."},{"id":"circ-04-starved-thermals","title":"Three GND pads receive only one of two required thermal spokes from the GND zone","location":"project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, F.Cu GND zone; pads C15.2 (107.85,98.76), U7.4 (101.01,102.68), C14.2 (101.59,104.29)","condition":"DRC error 'Thermal relief connection to zone incomplete (zone min spoke count 2; actual 1)' on the GND pads of decoupling caps C15/C14 and comparator U7 in the VR-module area, in the saved (unrefilled) zone fill.","mechanism":"A single-spoke thermal connection remains electrically connected (0 unconnected items) but halves the pad's copper connection, raising connection impedance for a comparator ground/decoupling path and reducing solder-joint and rework robustness; a refill or local keepout fix would be needed, which the read-only review cannot apply.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"three error-severity 'starved_thermal' entries listing Zone [GND] on F.Cu/B.Cu/In2.Gnd.Cu and pads C15.2, U7.4, C14.2"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"sections 1,3: independent DRC reproduction (same 3 starved_thermal errors) and triage"}],"reasoning":"Reproduced independently; connectivity is intact so impact is manufacturing robustness and marginally higher ground-connection impedance on small-signal parts, consistent with minor severity."},{"id":"circ-05-sheet-alias-duplicate","title":"Hierarchy resolved via byte-identical case-variant duplicate sheet file; divergence and case-collision hazard remains","location":"project/VR Conditioner.kicad_sch vs project/VR conditioner.kicad_sch; root reference at Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch line 21553","condition":"The candidate contains two sheet files whose names differ only by case, verified byte-identical (sha256 377a2691ec878301977100851c40e302b2b7864d88cc27c6c305c03bbf14e15b for both); the root schematic references 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' and the netlist resolves all VR-conditioner components through it.","mechanism":"The alias makes the 10-sheet hierarchy complete for this review (confirmed: U10/JP1/C23-C25/R25-R34 present in the netlist), but future edits through KiCad update only the referenced file, letting the lowercase copy silently go stale, and checkouts on case-insensitive filesystems (Windows/macOS defaults) will collide the two names. The packet itself declares this is a disposable alias and the original discrepancy remains open.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 6: matching sha256 of both files and root Sheetfile reference at line 21553"},{"path":"work/netlist/design.xml","locator":"sheet number 4 '/VR Conditioner/' with source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"components C23-C25, R25-R34, U10, JP1 with sheet '/VR Conditioner/'"}],"reasoning":"Verified the alias is a faithful byte copy and that connectivity is currently correct, so no electrical defect; recorded as info-level configuration-management concern consistent with the packet's declared limitation."},{"id":"circ-06-max9924-input-polarity","title":"VR1 (MAX9924) differential inputs wired with CRANK+ to IN- and CRANK- to IN+ (inverted vs. typical application)","location":"project/VR Conditioner.kicad_sch (U10 MAX9924, R25/R27 and R26/R28 input chains)","condition":"Netlist shows /CRANK + (J1.59) -> R25 4.7k -> R27 4.7k -> U10.2 (IN-) and /CRANK - (J1.55) -> R26 4.7k -> R28 4.7k -> U10.1 (IN+), the opposite of the MAX9924 typical application polarity.","mechanism":"Swapped differential polarity inverts the comparator output edge relative to the VR sensor's true tooth-edge zero crossing. ECU firmware edge selection can absorb a static inversion, and adaptive-threshold zero-cross detection is symmetric, so this does not necessarily impair function; but if firmware assumes the conventional polarity, trigger edges land on the wrong tooth flank, degrading timing accuracy on asymmetric VR waveforms.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets '/CRANK +': [J1.59, R25.2]; 'Net-(R25-Pad1)': [R25.1, R27.2]; 'Net-(U10-IN-)': [C23.1, R27.1, R29.2, U10.2]; '/CRANK -': [J1.55, R26.2]; 'Net-(U10-IN+)': [C23.2, R28.1, R29.1, U10.1]"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 5: MAX9924 wiring observation and rationale"}],"reasoning":"The cross-wiring is evidenced directly in the exported netlist, but no stated requirement fixes the intended polarity and the donor is an established design whose firmware pairing is out of scope, so this is recorded as an info-level concern for human confirmation rather than a defect."}]}}}
